{"path":"io/basic_osyncstream/emit","title":"std::basic_osyncstream<CharT,Traits,Allocator>::emit","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::basic_osyncstream&lt;CharT,Traits,Allocator&gt;::</span>emit","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/io/basic_osyncstream/emit","section":"io","kind":"page","summary":"Emits all buffered output and executes any pending flushes, by calling emit() on the underlying std::basic_syncbuf.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\">\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\"> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">void</span> emit<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Emits all buffered output and executes any pending flushes, by calling <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_syncbuf/emit\"><code>emit()</code></a> on the underlying <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_syncbuf\"><code>std::basic_syncbuf</code></a>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<p>(none)\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;syncstream&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_osyncstream\"><span class=\"kw2667\">std::<span class=\"me2\">osyncstream</span></span></a> bout<span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n        bout <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"Hello,\"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// no flush</span>\n        bout.<span class=\"me1\">emit</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// characters transferred; cout not flushed</span>\n        bout <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"World!\"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/manip/endl\"><span class=\"kw1808\">std::<span class=\"me2\">endl</span></span></a><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// flush noted; cout not flushed</span>\n        bout.<span class=\"me1\">emit</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// characters transferred; cout flushed</span>\n        bout <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"Greetings.\"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// no flush</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">}</span> <span class=\"co1\">// destructor calls emit(): characters transferred; cout not flushed</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"co1\">// emit can be used for local exception-handling on the wrapped stream</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_osyncstream\"><span class=\"kw2667\">std::<span class=\"me2\">osyncstream</span></span></a> bout<span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    bout <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"Hello, \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"World!\"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">try</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n        bout.<span class=\"me1\">emit</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">catch</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span>...<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n        <span class=\"co1\">// handle exceptions</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>Hello,\nWorld!\nGreetings.\nHello, World!</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div t-dsc-member-nobold-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_osyncstream/~basic_osyncstream\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>(destructor)</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  destroys the <code>basic_osyncstream</code> and emits its internal buffer <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_syncbuf/emit\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>emit</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  atomically transmits the entire internal buffer to the wrapped streambuf <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function of <code>std::basic_syncbuf&lt;CharT,Traits,Allocator&gt;</code>)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"io","title":"Input/output library"},{"path":"io/basic_osyncstream","title":"std::basic_osyncstream"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::basic_osyncstream<CharT,Traits,Allocator>::emit","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration. Emits all buffered output and executes any pending flushes, by calling emit() on the underlying std::basic_syncbuf."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"(none)"},{"label":"Example"},